{
  "id": "u05-l08b",
  "unit": "u05-numbers-time",
  "title": "Tomorrow, weeks & years",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**কাল** (*kal*) means **both 'tomorrow' and 'yesterday'**; the verb's tense tells you which. With no verb, as in **কাল শনিবার**, it means 'tomorrow'.\n\n**দিন** is any 'day' (**বার** is only for weekday names): **সাত দিন** 'seven days'.\n\nFor 'in' a span of time, add **-এ**: **সপ্তাহে** 'in a week', **বছরে** 'in a year': **এক বছরে বারো মাস**.\n\n**বছর** 'year' (**আমার বয়স বিশ বছর** 'I'm twenty years old'), **মাস** 'month', **প্রথম** 'first': **আজ আমার প্রথম দিন**.\n\nDon't mix up **মাস** (month), **মা** (mother) and **মাংস** (meat)!",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "kal",
      "bn": "কাল",
      "tr": "kal",
      "en": "tomorrow; yesterday",
      "notes": "Tense tells you which. To be explicit: আগামীকাল (agamikal) tomorrow, গতকাল (gotokal) yesterday."
    },
    {
      "id": "din-day",
      "bn": "দিন",
      "tr": "din",
      "en": "day"
    },
    {
      "id": "shoptahe",
